  "title": "He Faked Our Own Flyer To Price-Match Himself. We Noticed.",
  "script": "Forty dollars off\u2014again? At the hardware store, a regular tried to price-match a power drill using a photo of a competitor's flyer. He insisted their price was forty dollars less. I matched it without arguing\u2014store policy. A week later, he returned with the same flyer for another tool, then one with the same font and same crooked blue sale banner for a third item. I zoomed in on the competitor's logo. It was ours, mirrored and recolored in red. He agreed. He'd been editing our weekly ads and claiming they came from across town. I quietly printed every transaction from the past two months, checked our sale calendar, and gave the folder to my manager. He got banned from price-matching for a year. He still shops, paying full price loudly. Was the fake red logo worth a year?",
